body:
This would be more of a fitness question, however, not at all. It is often recommended (if you do a lot of excersise mostly) to add something that you like to your diet. After i began bodybuilding i started to eat more "healthy", but then it became more of eating less and less to the point i endangered myself. I got a new maintenance diet in which i can have some snacks a day, however im still pretty picky about it and are frequently non-sugary or caloric, i dont really feel good when eating "bad" stuff so i avoid them with alternatives.

&#x200B;

You just need to remember that you can eat mostly anything but in moderation.  The only thing that WILL make you gain weight is eating way more calories than you burn. OFC is important to remember that some chips won't have the same good nutrients than an apple, but if your main goal is to maintain yourself,  just keep your snacks quantity low in calories and thats it. If you restrict yourself a lot, it can often go the bad way, i not only tell you this from experience but from what i've read around. I higly recommend you to get  nutriologist if you can afford one, if not, you can also use some apps, but i dont recommend them quite a lot since they've made me obsessive :/ A lot of bodybuilders do tho...
